From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Mikhalitsyn <aleksandr.mikhalitsyn@futurfusion.io>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 20:08:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/nvme: add basic live migration support

It has some limitations:
- only one NVMe namespace is supported
- SMART counters are not preserved
- CMB is not supported
- PMR is not supported
- SPDM is not supported
- SR-IOV is not supported

Acked-by: Stefan Hajnoczi <stefanha@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexander Mikhalitsyn <aleksandr.mikhalitsyn@futurfusion.io>
Reviewed-by: Klaus Jensen <k.jensen@samsung.com>
Reviewed-by: Fabiano Rosas <farosas@suse.de>
Signed-off-by: Klaus Jensen <k.jensen@samsung.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9d378cab537d70d9e02edc11ff6ded7266c1078e)

[ backport to QEMU 10.0 by Lierfang:
  * 10.0 has no *_errp vmstate hooks: wrap the bool/Error ** hooks with
    NVME_VMSTATE_HOOK()/NVME_VMSTATE_POST_LOAD_HOOK() into int returning
    pre_load/pre_save/post_load hooks
  * 10.0 has no per-namespace atomic write parameters (NvmeNamespace.atomic,
    NvmeAtomic.atomic_boundary/atomic_nabo): drop them from the vmstate.
    As a result the NVMe migration stream is not compatible with upstream
    QEMU >= 10.1, only between QEMU 10.0 builds with this backport ]
